(i) from about 0.5% to about 5% by weight of a phospholipid component comprising hydrogenated phosphatidylcholine,
(ii) from about 2% to about 15% by weight of a fatty alcohol component comprising behenyl alcohol or a mixture of behenyl alcohol and cetyl alcohol,
(iii) from about 0.25% to about 2.5% by weight of a fatty acid component comprising behenic acid, and
(iv) from about 0.1% to about 5% by weight of an ester of a branched fatty acid and a branched fatty alcohol component comprising isostearylisostearate;

(e) 1% pramoxine, optionally as the pharmaceutically acceptable salt; and
(f) optionally a dermatologically acceptable excipient wherein the fatty alcohol and the phospholipid are present in a weight ratio of from about 10:1 to about 1:1; the fatty alcohol and the fatty acid are present in a weight ratio of from about 10:1 to about 1:1; and the fatty alcohol and the ester are present in a weight ratio of from about 10:1 to about 1:1; and wherein in use the composition has a water vapor transmission rate of less than about 65 gm−2 hr−1 measured in vitro using the modWVTR test methodology.

